# Input
```vue
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<template>
  <button @click="emit('change', 'foo', 'bar')">Change</button>
</template>

<script setup lang="ts">
const emit = defineEmits<{
  (e: "change", a: string, b: string): void;
}>();
</script>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid-template-setup-binding.vue:8:28 lint/nursery/useVueSingleEventPayload ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! The event change is declared with more than one value.
  
     6 │ <script setup lang="ts">
     7 │ const emit = defineEmits<{
   > 8 │   (e: "change", a: string, b: string): void;
       │                            ^^^^^^^^^
     9 │ }>();
    10 │ </script>
  
  i A listener written inline in a template, such as @change="onChange($event)", can only read the first value through $event. The other values are lost.
  
  i Put all the values in one object, and send that object instead.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

